# ── Pollinations.AI — no key needed · base: https://text.pollinations.ai/openai
#    note: no key and no account on the legacy host. The API that replaced it, gen.pollinations.ai, answers a keyless call with `401` `A valid API key is required. Get one at https://enter.pollinations.ai/keys` (2026-09-21); its keys spend Pollen, bought or earned from the site's Quests

# ── Arli AI — base: https://api.arliai.com/v1 · get a key: https://www.arliai.com/account
export ARLI_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: the quick-start calls it a drop-in OpenAI-API compatible endpoint and uses a placeholder model id; the catalog's names are the models page's, and the coding quick-start connects Roo Code and Kilo Code with a context window set to the model picked. /v1/chat/completions answers 401 without a key

# ── Bytez — base: https://api.bytez.com/models/v2/openai/v1 · get a key: https://bytez.com/api
export BYTEZ_API_KEY=""
#    note: model ids are Hugging Face ids, Qwen/Qwen3-4B being the docs' example; the OpenAI SDK examples pass the key as the api key and the docs' curl sends it bare in Authorization. /v1/models answers 401 without a key, and closed-source models need a provider key of your own

# ── Mixlayer — base: https://models.mixlayer.ai/v1 · get a key: https://console.mixlayer.com/app/api-keys
export MIXLAYER_API_KEY=""
#    note: the id is the pricing page's and the docs' own example; /v1/models answers 401 without a key, so it is not read off a catalog

# ── Yolo-Auto — base: https://yolo-auto.com/v1 · get a key: https://yolo-auto.com/app
export YOLO_AUTO_API_KEY=""
#    note: qwen3.8-flash is the one id the Free plan serves, "the recommended model for coding, text, and tool use" in the docs; qwen3.8-27b, the id this row carried until 2026-09-16, is still accepted from clients already configured with it, and yolo is a paid-only route whose server-side target can change. /v1/models and /v1/usage answer 401 without a key, and the free plan's context is 128K where Pro's is 256K

